1. e4 e6 {The only time I have played the French. I had played several school
games against Paul on Merseyside and as Black played the Marshall gambit. I
assumed he would be well prepared for that.} 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3
Ba5 {My preparation.} 6. b4 cxb4 7. Nb5 b3+ 8. c3 Bd7 9. Nd6+ Kf8 10. Qf3 $2
Be8 $2 (10... Qe7) 11. Bb5 Nc6 12. Bxc6 $2 bxc6 13. a4 Ne7 14. Ba3 Qb6 $2 (
14... Rb8) 15. Ne2 b2 $2 (15... Kg8) 16. Rb1 Qb3 17. Bxb2 Rb8 18. Qd3 f6 $4 (
18... Qa2) 19. Nxe8 Kxe8 20. O-O Kd7 21. exf6 gxf6 22. Nf4 e5 23. dxe5 fxe5 $2
(23... Bc7) 24. Qh3+ Ke8 25. Qh5+ Kd7 26. Qxe5 Bc7 27. Qe6+ Kd8 28. Rfe1 Re8
29. Nh5 d4 30. c4 Ba5 31. Nf6 Rb7 32. Red1 d3 33. Qd6+ Kc8 34. Nxe8 d2 35. Qe6+
Kd8 36. Nf6 Qd3 37. Qe4 Qd6 38. Qc2 Kc8 39. Qxh7 Qb4 40. Qh8+ Bd8 41. Qh3+ {
"A pretty poor game all round!" Sources: CHESS, March 1963, p190; D Ian W
Reynolds (2 January 2024)} 1-0

